From ca4ea2e562f61663ae8662714d954ab9a5545854 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Data-crea <sattler.daniel@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:25:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] OrionLayer Open Fix 112: the films on the wire, and their
 skip (SMACK::Play_Cinematic's frame loop calls no Get_Input, so nothing was
 sent while a film played and an injected click or key was never applied.
 ext::FilmGuard lives for the whole of Play_Cinematic: it reports the
 synthetic screen id 86 (SCREEN_EXT_FILM) and the film's file name, copied.
 ext::Film_Frame, once per pass of the loop after the frame is presented,
 records the frame and runs ext::Tick at most every 50 ms (k_film_tick_ms), so
 the client gets the film's picture (VISUAL) and the block "FILM", written
 last while a film plays: a version byte (1), uint8 the name's length and its
 bytes, int16 the frame smckplay last drew, int16 the total frames. The skip
 stays the original's own test, Keyboard_Status and Mouse_Button
 (smack.cpp:109-116): an injected key reaches the key queue as any key does;
 an injected click's release is held back while a film plays and pushed when
 the film ends, because both halves applied in one Pump_Game_Input_Queue leave
 Mouse_Button reading the release only. The film keeps its pacing: smckplay
 schedules each frame from the last frame's target, so a tick shorter than the
 frame's slack costs it nothing)

OrionLayer, open fix 112.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/extension-api.md |  2 +-
 src/ext/ext_api.cpp   | 65 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/ext/ext_api.h     | 41 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/game/smack.cpp    |  9 ++++++
 4 files changed, 115 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/extension-api.md b/docs/extension-api.md
index ce57bcf2..8fa80f4f 100644
--- a/docs/extension-api.md
+++ b/docs/extension-api.md
@@ -158,7 +158,7 @@ palette (256 x RGB).
 |---|---|---|
 | `ACTIVATE` 0x80 | int16 field index [, int16 x, y, x_end, y_end] | activates a field as if clicked; with the rectangle, only if the field there still is the one the client saw |
 | `INJECT_KEY` 0x81 | int16 key | a key press |
-| `INJECT_CLICK` 0x82 | int16 x, y | a left click at a point of the 640x480 screen |
+| `INJECT_CLICK` 0x82 | int16 x, y | a left click at a point of the 640x480 screen; while a film plays, the release follows when the film ends |
 | `CANCEL_FIELD` 0x83 | int16 field index | the right-button form of `ACTIVATE` |
 | `SET_JOBS` 0x84 | int16 colony, uint8 n, n x (uint8 pop, uint8 job) | sets colonists' jobs in one colony |
